{"name":"Chanoyu","hex":"#eee8d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chanoyu","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional Japanese tea ceremony in which matcha is prepared and presented."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chanoyu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Japanese tea ceremony","blocks":[{"text":"The Japanese tea ceremony is a cultural activity known as sadō/chadō  or chanoyu . The ceremony focuses on the presentation and serving of matcha (抹茶), powdered green tea; this procedure is called temae (点前). Much less commonly, Japanese tea practice uses leaf tea, primarily sencha. This practice is known as senchadō."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Chado.svg/330px-Chado.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_tea_ceremony","wikidata":"Q202298"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg/500px-Sen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg/1280px-Sen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Sen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg/500px-Sen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Master Sen no Rikyū, who codified the way of tea (painting by Hasegawa Tōhaku)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASen_no_Rikyu_JPN.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Kan%C5%8D_Osanobu_71_utaiawase.jpg/500px-Kan%C5%8D_Osanobu_71_utaiawase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Kan%C5%8D_Osanobu_71_utaiawase.jpg/1280px-Kan%C5%8D_Osanobu_71_utaiawase.jpg?utm_source